WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:03.550
(light music)

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:06.276
- I've been all over
this lake for 62 years.

00:00:06.276 --> 00:00:10.443
Never seen nothing like this
has happened in my lifetime.

00:00:11.801 --> 00:00:14.367
- [Man] Well, it's
certainly not our friend.

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:18.876
- Oh, they say it doubles in
size every four to five days.

00:00:18.876 --> 00:00:23.363
- And it has real long
tentacles under the water.

00:00:23.363 --> 00:00:26.690
- [Woman] It is literally a
monster that is overtaking

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:29.928
one of the most beautiful
places I've ever been.

00:00:29.928 --> 00:00:32.428
(light music)

00:00:34.406 --> 00:00:37.013
- [Man] The weevils are
the best bet because

00:00:37.013 --> 00:00:39.615
it's nature fighting nature.

00:00:39.615 --> 00:00:40.704
- If it wasn't for the weevils,

00:00:40.704 --> 00:00:42.735
we'd be in bad trouble right now.

00:00:42.735 --> 00:00:45.235
(light music)

00:00:51.936 --> 00:00:55.306
(light water splashing)

00:00:55.306 --> 00:00:57.806
(light music)

00:00:58.712 --> 00:01:00.548
- This is giant salvinia.

00:01:00.548 --> 00:01:03.591
Scientists call it the world's worst weed.

00:01:03.591 --> 00:01:05.937
On the surface it looks friendly enough.

00:01:05.937 --> 00:01:09.773
It's bright green, fuzzy,
and it has small oval leaves.

00:01:09.773 --> 00:01:13.190
But make no mistake, it is a lake killer.

00:01:14.402 --> 00:01:17.420
- Giant salvinia is an
invasive species from Brazil,

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:20.747
that first appeared in Texas in 1998.

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.958
Under ideal conditions, it
can cover 40 square miles

00:01:23.958 --> 00:01:25.935
in three months.

00:01:25.935 --> 00:01:27.856
Boats can't drive through it,

00:01:27.856 --> 00:01:30.176
native plants can't grow underneath it.

00:01:30.176 --> 00:01:34.568
And fish and other wildlife
struggle to survive.

00:01:34.568 --> 00:01:36.694
For twenty years we've
tried to get rid of it.

00:01:36.694 --> 00:01:39.938
Somebody even tried to kill
it with a blowtorch once.

00:01:39.938 --> 00:01:43.537
Today, we use an integrated
approach to manage salvinia,

00:01:43.537 --> 00:01:47.704
including a very small and
unique insect from Brazil.

00:01:48.925 --> 00:01:51.648
- By 2013, a group of
us became convinced that

00:01:51.648 --> 00:01:54.530
weevils help promise to
combat giant salvinia.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:56.890
So we organized a
grassroots effort to build

00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:00.581
a weevil greenhouse here
in Uncertain, Texas.

00:02:00.581 --> 00:02:02.696
- The main goal of the
greenhouse is to raise

00:02:02.696 --> 00:02:06.605
a large army of weevils with
a diet of fresh salvinia.

00:02:06.605 --> 00:02:09.440
And once their numbers
expand to a certain level,

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.938
then we'll take them out onto the lake.

00:02:12.938 --> 00:02:16.831
I've never raised bugs before,
and I'm not an entomologist.

00:02:16.831 --> 00:02:19.595
Everyone here is a volunteer,
and the reason we're

00:02:19.595 --> 00:02:23.030
doing this is because we care about the lake.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:26.197
Today, we have raised 350,000 weevils.

00:02:28.246 --> 00:02:32.722
This is not an easy find, but
it's worth trying to do this.

00:02:32.722 --> 00:02:35.625
They'll continue to do it,
I'll continue to do it,

00:02:35.625 --> 00:02:38.113
and most people down
here will continue to do

00:02:38.113 --> 00:02:40.181
what they can to save this lake.

00:02:40.181 --> 00:02:42.681
(light music)

00:02:45.986 --> 00:02:48.954
- We've had a few small areas of success.

00:02:48.954 --> 00:02:51.194
I grew up here in Pine Island Pond,

00:02:51.194 --> 00:02:54.924
and three years ago it
was covered in salvinia,

00:02:54.924 --> 00:02:56.992
but since the release of the weevils,

00:02:56.992 --> 00:02:59.835
we've seen slow, but dramatic change.

00:02:59.835 --> 00:03:02.724
(light music)

00:03:02.724 --> 00:03:04.771
- [Robert] Caddo Lake
is a unique treasure.

00:03:04.771 --> 00:03:07.077
I've fallen in it, I've swam in it,

00:03:07.077 --> 00:03:09.196
I've fished and hunted in it.

00:03:09.196 --> 00:03:13.363
This lake has been part of
my soul for almost 50 years.

00:03:14.504 --> 00:03:17.151
Fighting the salvinia is not an easy task.

00:03:17.151 --> 00:03:19.501
It's not glamorous or flashy.

00:03:19.501 --> 00:03:21.279
But the men and women who fight it

00:03:21.279 --> 00:03:22.863
have no intention of losing.

00:03:22.863 --> 00:03:26.375
And at the end of the day, we're
all in it for the long run.

00:03:26.375 --> 00:03:28.875
(light music)

